ifferent vendors (GE, Philips, Siemens, etc.), scanning protocol"}, {"index": 32, "kind": "p", "section_ids": ["S1", null, null], "preview": "Motivated by the observed heterogeneity in medical imaging data, we propose a deep stacked transformation data augmentation approach (called"}, {"index": 33, "kind": "p", "section_ids": ["S1", null, null], "preview": "BigAug is designed to have individual images undergo nine stacked image transformations within each training iteration, in order to substant"}, {"index": 34, "kind": "li", "section_ids": ["S1", null, null], "preview": "systematically analyze the effect of each augmentation technique on the model’s generalization ability, revealing the major differences of m"}, {"index": 35, "kind": "li", "section_ids": ["S1", null, null], "preview": "demonstrate BigAug to be uniformly effective for both MRI and ultrasound, with 11.6% average reduction in Dice coefficient on unseen domains"}, {"index": 36, "kind": "li", "section_ids": ["S1", null, null], "preview": "demonstrate BigAug to outperform “shallower” stacked transforms (with less transforms) on unseen domains, and modest improvement compared to"}, {"index": 37, "kind": "li", "section_ids": ["S1", null, null], "preview": "show that when trained with datasets of the same size, the model with BigAug can achieve a similar performance on the unseen domain as compa"}, {"index": 38, "kind": "li", "section_ids": ["S1", null, null], "preview": "show that BigAug is a key component for achieving good generalization and state-of-the-art segmentation accuracy on several unseen (public) "}, {"index": 39, "kind": "h2", "section_ids": ["S2", null, null], "preview": "II. Methods"}, {"index": 40, "kind": "p", "section_ids": ["S2", null, null], "preview": "We consider the problem of unseen domain generalization, where we are provided with data X S and annotations Y S from a single source domain"}, {"index": 41, "kind": "h3", "section_ids": ["S3", "S2", null, null], "preview": "A. Deep Stac